# Dashboard — environment configuration
#
# Copy to `.env.local` (gitignored) and edit. Every variable below is
# optional: the documented default applies when it is unset, and an
# unparsable value falls back to that same default with a warning on the
# console rather than failing the build or crashing at startup.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A NOTE ON THE `VITE_` PREFIX — READ BEFORE ADDING ANYTHING HERE
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Vite inlines every variable beginning with `VITE_` into the JavaScript
# bundle at build time. They are not secrets, they are not hidden, and they
# are not fetched at runtime — they are literal strings in a file anyone can
# download and read.
#
# Never put a credential, API key, token, connection string, or password
# behind a `VITE_` prefix. Anything genuinely secret belongs to the backend,
# which reads it from `dotnet user-secrets` or a plain (unprefixed)
# environment variable and never sends it to the browser.
#
# As it happens, none of the variables below are secret — which is why they
# are all safe to commit as examples.


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Frontend (frontend/)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Where the app's data comes from.
#
#   api  — talk to the ASP.NET Core backend over HTTP. The real application.
#   demo — run the .NET Application and Domain assemblies in the browser via
#          WebAssembly, against an in-memory generated fixture. No backend,
#          no database, no network calls. What the public demo is built with.
#
# Anything else falls back to `api` with a console warning. It deliberately
# does not guess at typos: silently selecting the wrong data source is the one
# mistake this must never make on your behalf.
#
# Default: api
VITE_DATA_SOURCE=api

# Base URL of the backend API. Ignored entirely when VITE_DATA_SOURCE=demo.
# Trailing slashes are stripped. An unparsable URL falls back to the default.
#
# Default: http://localhost:5199
VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:5199

# The path the app is served from, for hosts that serve a project from a
# subdirectory. A GitHub Pages project page lives at /<repo>/; a local dev
# server and a user/organisation Pages site live at /.
#
# This is the single source for the base path. Vite's `base` is set from it at
# build time and re-exposed at runtime as `import.meta.env.BASE_URL`, which is
# what the router's basename is derived from — so the bundler and the router
# cannot drift apart and leave you with working assets and 404 routes.
#
# Default: /
# VITE_BASE_PATH=/Dashboard/

# Build identification, shown in the app footer so a deployed page can be tied
# back to a commit. Both are filled in automatically — the commit from
# `git rev-parse`, the timestamp at build time — and fall back to "dev" when
# git is unavailable. Set them explicitly only in a build environment that has
# no git history, such as a source tarball.
#
# VITE_COMMIT=
# VITE_BUILT_AT=


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Backend (backend/src/Dashboard.Api)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# These are NOT read from this file — ASP.NET Core reads configuration from
# appsettings.json, user-secrets, and the process environment. They are
# documented here so that every knob in the system is described in one place.

# PostgreSQL connection string. REQUIRED to run the API; there is no default,
# and the app fails with an explicit message if it is missing.
#
# This is the one genuine secret in the project. Set it with user-secrets in
# development so it never touches the working tree:
#
#   cd backend/src/Dashboard.Api
#   dotnet user-secrets set "ConnectionStrings:Dashboard" \
#     "Host=localhost;Database=vantage_dev;Username=<user>;Password=<password>"
#
# In a hosted environment, set the environment variable instead. Note the
# double underscore — that is how .NET maps a flat variable onto the nested
# `ConnectionStrings:Dashboard` key.
#
# ConnectionStrings__Dashboard=Host=localhost;Database=vantage_dev;Username=...;Password=...

# Which appsettings.{Environment}.json layers in, and whether migrations and
# development seeding run at startup. Only `Development` seeds.
#
# Default: Production
# ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT=Development
